ety & Cine Club Committee\nCell for SC/ST/OBC/MOBC/Minority\nGreen & Clean Campus Committee\nStudent Mentoring Committee\nInternal Complaints Committee (ICC)\nDownloads\nOFFLINE ADMISSION FORM\nEXAMINATION PROGRAMME\nREGISTRATION FORM HS-2023-24\nINTER COLLEGE YOUTH FESTIVAL, 2023-24\nNCC Enrolment Form (Girls')\nSelf declaration form\nHS Exam Form-2025\nDepartment of Botany\nProfile\nFaculty\nEvents\nHistory:\nLTK College was established on 22\nnd\nAugust 1977 with only an arts stream at the initiative of the local people. In 1994, the Science stream was established with the demands of the present modern age. The local people were encouraged to open the science stream in spite of economic paucity in the institution. In 1994 Science stream offers two years of higher secondary certificate courses in six subjects and established a three-year degree course in 1996 with the permission of Dibrugarh University. The Science stream was provincialized under the New Assam College Provincialization Act 2013 w.e.f. 14/08/2013. From 2006-2007 Botany department started the major course and was able to show good results. Since the establishment of the major subject in the botany department 13 batches have successfully completed B.Sc. in Botany Major with 1\nst\nClass and 2\nnd\nclass. The pass percentage of our department was good. Some of our students completed P.G. Course and completed State Eligibility Test (Life Science). One of our students pursuing a Ph.D. at Cotton University in the Department of Botany.\nBotany Department has an Orchidarium with 40 orchid species having medicinal value. This Orchidarium was established in 2016. In 2014 one medicinal plant garden with 64 numbers of plant species was established. Orchidarium and medicinal plant garden are the beauty of the Botany department. It is the use of plants for medicinal purposes and the uses of such uses.\nMission:\nThe mission of our department is to foster an environment of excellence by attracting and supporting the outstanding students, faculty, and staff needed to sustain our vision.\nVision:\nThe vision of our department is to conduct innovative research, teaching and outreach on the patterns and processes of life with a focus on plants and their environments.\nSeat Capacity :\nHS\n150\nB.Sc. (Honours)\n50\nB.Sc. (Generic)\n50\nSyllabus :\nView/download\nAchievement :\nView/download\nDepartment Activities :\nView/download\nMentoring (Mentor - Mentee) List :\nView/download\nField Study/ Tour :\nView/download\nTotal Alumni 2017-22:\n(Department Alumni Whatsapp Group)\nhttps://chat.whatsapp.com/JwOv4kIvTdDI9ydvi4hwUz\nYEAR\nTotal Alumni\n2016-17\n9\n2017-18\n18\n2018-19\n28\n2019-20\n41\n2020-21\n38\nDepartmental stock book 2017-2022:\nCollege has been purchase Laboratory chemical reagent equipment books etc and department always maintain one stock book. (Xerox copy enclosed)\nDepartmental E-content :\nView/download\nWebinar :\nDepartment of botany\norganize\ntwo number of Webinars in Covid Period.\nAbout forest man of India,\nPadma Shri\nJadav Payeng\nStudent Capability Enhancement Program (ADD-on course) :\nView/download\nFaculty Programme:\nView/download\nName\nDesignation\nQualification\nDate of Joining\nView Profile\nBHARAT HAZARIKA\nAssistant Professor\nM.Sc., M.Phil\n06-Nov-1995\nView Profile\nJULLY GOHAIN NEOG\nAssistant Professor (HOD)\nM.Sc., M.Phil\n05-Mar-1997\nView Profile\nPRABHAT SAIKIA\nAssistant Professor\nM.Sc., M.Phil, B.Ed.\n03-Sep-2003\nView Profile\nJADUMONI SAIKIA\nGuest Faculty\nM. Sc.\n01-Oct-2019\nView Profile\njkg\n22-Aug-2024\nView Profile\nQuick Links\nUGC\nNAAC\nIGNOU\nVIDYA LAKSHMI\nDIBRUGARH UNIVERSITY\nExplore\nGAUHATI UNIVERSITY\nTEZPUR UNIVERSITY\nAHSEC\nDHE,ASSAM\nGOVT. OF ASSAM\nदिव्यांगों के लिए\nLakhimpur Telahi Kamalabaria College | লক্ষীমপুৰ তেলাহী কমলাবৰীয়া মহাবিদ্যালয়\nAzad, Lakhimpur, Assam-787031\nPhone : (+91) 0375-223-0119\nEmail : ltkcollege@yahoo.in\nCopyright © 2025 Lakhimpur Telahi Kamalabaria College. All Rights Reserved\n